Source: https://github.com/apache/superset; its description of its own API
(the OpenAPI document a Superset serves at /api/v1/_openapi) as the file
superset.spec.json in https://github.com/Winding2020/superset-mcp at ff8e0eb
(MIT per its package.json) and, with the same bytes, in
https://github.com/aptro/superset-mcp at b3dd425 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025
Aptro).

What is taken from it here: the HTTP method and path of each of the 210
methods of that description, with the part of the API each belongs to
(internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/superset_methods.json). Nothing else of
the description is kept. The catalog of actions made from that list is
Hypomnema's own (internal/controlplane/serviceproxy/superset.go).

What is learned from the two MCP servers, with no code of theirs copied: how
a local account signs in, that a request refused for its token signs in again,
and what a request that is not a GET carries (their src/client/base-client.ts
and main.py); how a chart is read with its dashboard's filters (their
src/client/dashboard-client.ts). The Go that does this is in
internal/controlplane/integration/account.go and internal/controlplane/superset.
